Subject: Cantor Phase3 Strict Pure Machine Forms Exploded Specification

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Strict_Pure_Machine_Forms.sop

& [TypeAxis] is closed enums and deny-unknown structs
  + [artifact] is typed digest reference
  + [mutation] is stage and transition
  + [seal_review] is stage and transition
  + [fault] is consequence
  + [strength] is consistency and immutability
  + [path] is before-and-after regular-file evidence
  + [review] is check and disposition

& [PurityAxis] is compile-time inspectable
  + [allowed_imports] is serde and thiserror plus standard collections
  + [forbidden_imports] is fs, process, net, time, env, random, key, database, and provider clients
  + [unsafe] is absent

& [TransitionAxis] is exhaustive
  + [test] iterates every ordered pair of stages
  + [accepted] equals the canonical edge set
  + [rejected] returns typed invalid_transition

& [ChangeAxis] is table-driven
  + [add] is none to some
  + [modify] is some to different some
  + [delete] is some to none
  + [mode_change] is some to same-byte different-mode some
  + [all_other_shapes] reject

& [ReviewAxis] preserves epistemic distinctions
  + [unknown] is not fail
  + [not_applicable] may omit evidence
  + [pass_fail_unknown] require evidence
  + [eligible] is only a Phase3D consideration edge

& [VerificationAxis] is proportional
  + [unit] is scalar, path, transition, consequence, change, evidence, and JSON tests
  + [API_scan] is no forbidden method or import
  + [global] is all prior debug and release tests, lint, docs, audit, and evidence
